.TH PATH_COMMON_PREFIX 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
path_common_prefix \- Find the common prefix between two paths

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/path_internal.h>
.IB #include <lib/byte.h>

.IB SizePair
.IB path_common_prefix(const char* s1, size_t n1, const char* s2, size_t n2);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpath_common_prefix\fR function finds the common prefix between two paths. It compares the components of the paths and returns the lengths of the common parts.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB s1
The first input path string.
.TP
.IB n1
The length of the first input path string.
.TP
.IB s2
The second input path string.
.TP
.IB n2
The length of the second input path string.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns a structure of type \fBSizePair\fR, which contains the lengths of the common prefix components in the two paths.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBpath_common_prefix\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/path_internal.h>
#include <lib/byte.h>

int main() {
    const char* path1 = "/usr/lib";
    const char* path2 = "/usr/include";
    SizePair result = path_common_prefix(path1, strlen(path1), path2, strlen(path2));
    printf("Common prefix length: %zu\n", result.sz1);
    return 0;
}
.nef